      "narrative": {
        "text": "'Current Immunization schedule': a grid with one row per vaccine and one column per age (Birth, 6 wks, 10 wks, 14 wks, 5 mo, 6 mo, 7 mo, 8 mo, 9 mo, 12 mo, 15 mo, 18 mo, 22 mo, 24 mo, 10 Yrs, 15-49 Yrs). Dose numbers by row: BCG 1 at birth; Hep B birth dose 1 at birth; Oral polio 0 at birth, 1 at 6 wks, 2 at 10 wks, 3 at 14 wks; DTP-HepB-Hib (penta) 1, 2, 3 at 6, 10, 14 wks; PCV 1, 2, 3 at 6, 10, 14 wks; Rotavirus 1, 2, 3 at 6, 10, 14 wks; Inactivated Polio 1 at 6 wks and 2 at 14 wks; Measles-Rubella 1 at 9 mo and 2 at 18 mo; Yellow Fever 1 at 9 mo; Malaria (row label in red) 1, 2, 3 at 6, 7, 8 mo and 4 at 18 mo; Vitamin A 1 at 6 mo, 2 at 12 mo, 3 at 18 mo, 4 at 24 mo; Deworming 1 at 12 mo; HPV 1 at 10 Yrs; Tetanus Diphtheria (TD) '1,2,3,4 &5' at 15-49 Yrs. The 5 mo, 15 mo and 22 mo columns are empty. Cell shading follows the slide's legend (slide text): dark grey 'previous on schedule'; light blue 'Newly introduced' (Hep B birth dose, IPV 1, Rotavirus 3, Measles-Rubella 2, Yellow Fever); orange 'Yet to be introduced' (Malaria 1 to 4, HPV).",
